QNX 8.0 has alsa-lib, not QSA -- do not force the QSA audio backend.

CMakeLists.txt selects src/audio/qnx unconditionally for QNX.  That
backend is written against <sys/asoundlib.h> and snd_pcm_open_preferred(),
the QNX 6.x/7.x sound API.  QNX 8.0 replaced QSA with a real alsa-lib, so
the header does not exist and the build stops at:

    src/audio/qnx/SDL_qsa_audio.c:37:10: fatal error:
        sys/asoundlib.h: No such file or directory

CheckALSA() runs a few lines later and finds the alsa-lib that QNX 8 does
ship, so the generic ALSA backend covers this platform properly.  Gating
the QSA block on QNX_USE_QSA_AUDIO keeps it available for older QNX
releases without breaking QNX 8.  Same change as the SDL2 recipe here.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1562,7 +1562,14 @@
         set(SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER_NETBSD 1)
         sdl_glob_sources("${SDL3_SOURCE_DIR}/src/audio/netbsd/*.c")
         set(HAVE_SDL_AUDIO TRUE)
-    elseif(QNX)
+    elseif(QNX AND QNX_USE_QSA_AUDIO)
+        # src/audio/qnx is the QSA backend: it includes <sys/asoundlib.h> and
+        # calls snd_pcm_open_preferred(), the QNX 6.x/7.x sound API.  QNX 8.0
+        # replaced QSA with a real alsa-lib -- <alsa/asoundlib.h>, libasound.so
+        # -- so this file does not compile there.  CheckALSA() immediately
+        # below picks the generic ALSA backend, which is the correct one for
+        # QNX 8.  Set QNX_USE_QSA_AUDIO=ON to build the old backend on an
+        # older QNX.
         set(SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER_QNX 1)
         sdl_glob_sources("${SDL3_SOURCE_DIR}/src/audio/qnx/*.c")
         sdl_link_dependency(asound LIBS asound)
